{"path":"keyword/union","title":"C++ keyword: union","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">C++ keyword:</span><code>union</code>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/keyword/union","section":"keyword","kind":"index","summary":"","html":"<h3 id=\"Usage\">Usage</h3>\n<ul><li> <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/union\"> declaration of a union type</a>\n</li><li> If a function or a variable exists in scope with the name identical to the name of a union type, <code>union</code> can be prepended to the name for disambiguation, resulting in an <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/elaborated_type_specifier\">elaborated type specifier</a>\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<ul><li> <a href=\"/w/cpp/keyword/class\"><code>class</code></a>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/keyword/struct\"><code>struct</code></a>\n</li></ul>\n<table class=\"t-rev-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-rev t-since-cxx11\"><td>\n<ul><li> <a href=\"/w/cpp/identifier_with_special_meaning/final\"><code>final</code></a>\n</li></ul>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span></td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Usage","id":"Usage"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"keyword","title":"C++ keywords"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"C++ keyword: union","children":[{"label":"Usage"},{"label":"See also"}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":48,"codeBlockCount":0}
